{"path":"error/exception","title":"std::exception","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>exception","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/error/exception","section":"error","kind":"page","summary":"Provides consistent interface to handle errors through the throw expression.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/exception\">&lt;exception&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">class</span> exception<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Provides consistent interface to handle errors through the <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/throw\">throw expression</a>. \n</p><p>All exceptions generated by the standard library inherit from <code>std::exception</code>.\n</p>\n<table class=\"t-rev-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-rev t-since-cxx26\"><td>\n<p>All member functions of <code>std::exception</code> are <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span></span>.\n</p>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(since C++26)</span></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Member_functions\">Member functions</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div t-dsc-member-nobold-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/exception/exception\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>(constructor)</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  constructs the exception object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div t-dsc-member-nobold-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/exception/~exception\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>(destructor)</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[virtual]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  destroys the exception object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(virtual public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/exception/operator=\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator=</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  copies exception object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/exception/what\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>what</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[virtual]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns an explanatory string <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(virtual public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Standard_exception_requirements\">Standard exception requirements</h3>\n<p>Each standard library class <code>T</code> that derives from <code>std::exception</code> has the following publicly accessible member functions, each of them <span class=\"t-rev-inl t-until-cxx11\"><span>do not exit with an exception</span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx11\">(until C++11)</span></span></span><span class=\"t-rev-inl t-since-cxx11\"><span>having a <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/noexcept_spec\">non-throwing exception specification</a></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span></span></span>:\n</p>\n<ul><li> <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/default_constructor\">default constructor</a> (unless other constructors are provided)\n</li><li> <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/copy_constructor\">copy constructor</a>\n</li><li> <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/as_operator\">copy assignment operator</a>\n</li></ul>\n<p>The copy constructor and the copy assignment operator meet the following postcondition:\n</p>\n<ul><li> If two objects <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">lhs</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">rhs</span></code> both have dynamic type <code>T</code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">lhs</span></code> is a copy of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">rhs</span></code>, then <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/byte/strcmp\"><span class=\"kw1153\">std::<span class=\"me2\">strcmp</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>lhs.<span class=\"me1\">what</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, rhs.<span class=\"me1\">what</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is equal to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code>.\n</li></ul>\n<p>The <code>what()</code> member function of each such <code>T</code> satisfies the constraints specified for <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/exception/what\">std::exception::what()</a></span>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Standard_exceptions\">Standard exceptions</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/logic_error\"><code>logic_error</code></a>\n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/invalid_argument\"><code>invalid_argument</code></a>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/domain_error\"><code>domain_error</code></a>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/length_error\"><code>length_error</code></a>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/out_of_range\"><code>out_of_range</code></a>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future_error\"><code>future_error</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span>\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/runtime_error\"><code>runtime_error</code></a>\n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/range_error\"><code>range_error</code></a>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/overflow_error\"><code>overflow_error</code></a>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/underflow_error\"><code>underflow_error</code></a>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/regex/regex_error\"><code>regex_error</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/system_error\"><code>system_error</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span>\n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/failure\"><code>ios_base::failure</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/filesystem/filesystem_error\"><code>filesystem::filesystem_error</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span>\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/tx_exception\"><code>tx_exception</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-tm-ts t-mark-ts\">(TM TS)</span>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/nonexistent_local_time\"><code>nonexistent_local_time</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/ambiguous_local_time\"><code>ambiguous_local_time</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/format/format_error\"><code>format_error</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span>\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/bad_typeid\"><code>bad_typeid</code></a>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/bad_cast\"><code>bad_cast</code></a>\n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/any/bad_any_cast\"><code>bad_any_cast</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span>\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/optional/bad_optional_access\"><code>bad_optional_access</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/expected/bad_expected_access\"><code>bad_expected_access</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/bad_weak_ptr\"><code>bad_weak_ptr</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/bad_function_call\"><code>bad_function_call</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_alloc\"><code>bad_alloc</code></a>\n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_array_new_length\"><code>bad_array_new_length</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span>\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/bad_exception\"><code>bad_exception</code></a>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/failure\"><code>ios_base::failure</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx11\">(until C++11)</span>\n</li><li><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/variant/bad_variant_access\"><code>bad_variant_access</code></a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span>\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<table class=\"wikitable ftm-begin ftm-has-value\">\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/feature_test\">Feature-test</a> macro\n</th>\n<th><abbr>Value</abbr>\n</th>\n<th><abbr>Std</abbr>\n</th>\n<th>Feature\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/feature_test#cpp_lib_constexpr_exceptions\"><code>__cpp_lib_constexpr_exceptions</code></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/compiler_support/26#cpp_lib_constexpr_exceptions_202411L\"><code>202411L</code></a></td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark\">(C++26)</span></td>\n<td><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span></span> for exception types\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue471\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 471</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++98\n</td>\n<td>there was no requirement on standard library classes derived from <code>std::exception</code>\n</td>\n<td>added\n</td></tr></table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Member functions","id":"Member_functions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Standard exception requirements","id":"Standard_exception_requirements"},{"depth":3,"text":"Standard exceptions","id":"Standard_exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"error","title":"Diagnostics library"}],"children":[{"path":"error/exception/exception","title":"std::exception::exception"},{"path":"error/exception/operator=","title":"std::exception::operator="},{"path":"error/exception/what","title":"std::exception::what"},{"path":"error/exception/~exception","title":"std::exception::~exception"}],"map":{"label":"std::exception","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Provides consistent interface to handle errors through the throw expression."},{"label":"Member functions","children":[{"label":"(constructor)","note":"constructs the exception object"},{"label":"(destructor)","note":"destroys the exception object"},{"label":"operator=","note":"copies exception object"},{"label":"what","note":"returns an explanatory string"}]},{"label":"Standard exception requirements","note":"Each standard library class T that derives from std::exception has the following publicly accessible member functions, each of them do not exit with an…"},{"label":"Standard exceptions"},{"label":"Notes"}]},"standards":["C++11","C++17","C++20","C++23","C++26"],"wordCount":285,"codeBlockCount":0}
